# Siddur performance — hot-path rules

Any siddur change (pack JSON, English translation, liturgy gate, solo/minyan filter, specialize logic) must follow the performance patterns already in this codebase. The reader runs over **every leaf** at assemble/specialize time — avoid work that scales with scroll or recompiles regex per step.

## Hot paths (do not slow these down)

- `SiddurAssembler.assemble` → `SiddurInsertText.specialize` on each block
- `SiddurLiturgyEnglish.polish` / `expandLeaderSayCues` (every leaf with English — **including Selichot**)
- `SiddurCommunalText`, `SiddurHallelText`, `SiddurAshreiText`, and other `*Text.kt` specialists
- Reader filters (`SiddurSoloMode`, `SiddurMinyanNotes` step cues) when toggling solo mode

## Required patterns

1. **Cheap gate first** — `contains`, `in`, or blank checks on block id/title before touching body text.
2. **Precompiled regex** — `private val FOO = Regex(...)` on the object; never `Regex(...)` inside per-step/per-block loops.
3. **Hebrew matching** — prefer `lettersOnly()` / nikud-stripped plain strings + `indexOf`, not regex on full nikud text.
4. **Return unchanged** — if nothing mutated, return the same `SiddurBlock` / `SiddurLiturgyStep` instance (see `SiddurLiturgyEnglish.polish`).
5. **English cleanup** — new Selichot / dump / stage-direction patterns belong in `SiddurLiturgyEnglish` (or the right `*Text.kt`), with a `needsX()` gate so untouched blocks skip work entirely.

## When adding English needles (Selichot, Half Hallel, Kaddish, etc.)

- Add **compiled** patterns + a cheap substring gate (`en.contains("…")`) before regex.
- Widen needles in the existing specialist (`SiddurHallelText`, `SiddurMinyanNotes`, `SiddurSoloMode`) — do not add one-off scans in UI composables.
- Verify with a **pack-backed** test block, not a toy stub.

## Anti-patterns (do not introduce)

- `Regex(...)` inside `map`/`forEach` over steps or blocks
- Re-lowercasing or re-filtering the same string multiple times in one function
- Full-text regex over multi-KB mega-blocks when id/title or a short prefix gate would suffice
- New per-frame string work in `SiddurReaderDialog` — filter in `remember(...)` keys, not in lazy list item lambdas without caching

Reference implementation: `SiddurLiturgyEnglish` header comment and `SiddurInsertText` top-level `private val` regex fields.
